1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,111
It's my fourth day in saudi arabia I really enjoyed the bustling city life of jeddah but now the real adventure begins.
这是我在沙特阿拉伯的第四天。我很享受吉达热闹的城市生活，但现在，真正的冒险开始了。

2
00:00:07,121 --> 00:00:10,640
My friend sarah and I flew to a very remote district called kasim.
我的朋友 Sarah 和我飞到一个非常偏远、叫“kasim”的地区。

3
00:00:10,640 --> 00:00:14,711
And met up with a local friend named matib who knows everything about the life up here.
我们在那里见到一位叫“matib”的当地朋友，他对这一带的生活了如指掌。

4
00:00:14,721 --> 00:00:20,960
Together we drove several hours in search of the bed winds across the sand dunes into the middle of nowhere.
我们一起开车好几个小时，穿越沙丘，寻找“bed winds”（字幕如此），来到偏僻的荒野。

5
00:00:20,960 --> 00:00:25,960
Oh my god are we gonna make it that's a very steep way.
天啊，我们能过去吗？这条路可真陡。

6
00:00:27,121 --> 00:00:35,350
We've been driving for two hours through white sand we've driven through orange sand yellow sand some places that look like mars.
我们已在白沙中开了两个小时，还穿过橙沙、黄沙，有些地方看起来就像火星。

7
00:00:35,360 --> 00:00:42,471
And we are just now rolling up to a bedouin camp to meet some bedouins to experience the life to see how they live.
现在终于抵达一个贝都因营地，去见一些贝都因人，体验生活，看看他们怎样过日子。

8
00:00:42,481 --> 00:00:45,441
I'm excited you're gonna live the entire day that's been doing.
我很兴奋。对方说：“你会在这里过完整天，that's been doing”（字幕后半句不清）。

9
00:00:45,441 --> 00:00:48,710
You're gonna do everything you're gonna be with me too.
“你什么都要做，还会和我在一起。”

10
00:00:48,720 --> 00:00:54,641
Sarah where are we in the middle of the desert and lots of camels surrounded by camels.
Sarah，我们在哪里？在沙漠中央，还有好多骆驼，被骆驼包围着。

11
00:00:54,641 --> 00:01:01,591
We have made it to the desert in the sand dunes we're surrounded by camels this is the life.
我们到了沙丘里的沙漠，被骆驼包围。这才叫生活啊。

12
00:01:01,601 --> 00:01:07,161
It's a friendly one they love to touch them from here it's like a dog you put them like under the neck.
这只很友善。它们喜欢你摸这里，就像狗一样，摸脖子下方。

13
00:01:07,281 --> 00:01:11,680
If he doesn't have food he would have from the fat that he has in hump.
如果它没有食物，就会利用驼峰里的脂肪。

14
00:01:11,680 --> 00:01:14,241
Tell me about where we are right now in saudi arabia.
说说我们现在位于沙特阿拉伯的什么地方。

15
00:01:14,241 --> 00:01:20,151
We are actually in the middle of saudi arabia in a region of kasim that sits in the middle of arabian peninsula.
我们其实在沙特中部，一个位于阿拉伯半岛中部、叫“kasim”的地区。

16
00:01:20,161 --> 00:01:27,361
What's it known for kasim is famous of date palms farmers and also desert as you see a lot of camels around here.
这里以什么闻名？“kasim”以椰枣树、农民，还有沙漠闻名；你看，这里有很多骆驼。

17
00:01:27,361 --> 00:01:36,641
Because their ancestors used to use it for uh trading and they drink the milk and they sometimes use them also for transportation and between tribes as well.
因为祖先过去用骆驼做贸易，喝骆驼奶，有时还用它们运输，也用于部落之间。

18
00:01:36,641 --> 00:01:40,150
If I want to buy a camel how much does it cost.
如果我想买一头骆驼，要花多少钱？

19
00:01:40,160 --> 00:01:46,240
50 000 40 000 15 000 to 20 30.
五万、四万、一万五到二十、三十（报价数字按字幕保留，单位和完整范围不明确）。

20
00:01:46,240 --> 00:01:49,440
I want you to tell him that when I was in mauritania which is in west africa.
我想让你告诉他，我在西非的毛里塔尼亚时，

21
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:53,841
I bought a camel like this size for 450 us dollars.
买过一头差不多这么大的骆驼，花了四百五十美元。

22
00:01:53,841 --> 00:01:58,150
Okay he can't believe it it's like impossible camels are really expensive.
好，他不敢相信，觉得简直不可能。骆驼真的很贵。

23
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:02,800
It means a lot to us it's not just uh animal for them it's more than animal.
这对我们意义重大。对他们来说，它不只是动物，比动物更有分量。

24
00:02:02,800 --> 00:02:07,991
That was pretty nice thank you so much.
这真好，非常感谢。

25
00:02:08,001 --> 00:02:13,520
We made our way onwards across the dunes in search of more bedouins who are living in this vast landscape.
我们继续向前，穿过沙丘，寻找生活在这片辽阔景观中的更多贝都因人。

26
00:02:13,520 --> 00:02:19,751
Little did I know that we would stumble across an ancient and unknown world wonder.
我当时根本不知道，我们竟会偶然遇上一处古老、鲜为人知的世界奇观。

27
00:02:19,761 --> 00:02:24,880
Wow we just rolled up in the middle of the sand dunes and we found an abandoned town.
哇，我们刚来到沙丘中央，发现了一座废弃的小镇。

28
00:02:24,880 --> 00:02:32,631
Where are we right now we are in the middle of the desert as you see we're surrounded by huge dunes.
我们现在在哪里？在沙漠中央，正如你看到的，周围全是巨大的沙丘。

29
00:02:32,641 --> 00:02:37,761
There are date palms the date palms are the source for the people who lived in there.
这里有椰枣树；对过去生活在这里的人来说，椰枣树是生活来源。

30
00:02:37,761 --> 00:02:40,321
Do we know how how old these houses are.
我们知道这些房子有多老吗？

31
00:02:40,321 --> 00:02:50,001
Uh there is no archaeological study to this site but people left it almost 50 years ago when you know people started to have easier life somewhere else.
还没有针对这个遗址的考古研究，但约五十年前人们离开了，当时大家开始在别处过上更轻松的生活。

32
00:02:50,001 --> 00:02:56,321
Why do you think they chose this spot to live here because there is water of course that's the source for you know starting life.
你觉得他们为什么选这个地方居住？当然是因为有水，那是开始生活的源头。

33
00:02:56,321 --> 00:03:03,440
And there is still surrounding the area as you see the date palms are still green because there is still water underneath of them.
而且周围仍然有——你看，椰枣树还是绿的，因为它们下面仍然有水。

34
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:07,281
How on earth is there water in a really hot climate in the desert.
到底怎么会在沙漠这么热的气候里有水呢？

35
00:03:07,281 --> 00:03:11,281
We see it hot on the surface but it's still wet underneath.
我们看到地表很热，但下面仍然是湿的。

36
00:03:11,281 --> 00:03:14,001
I wouldn't mind living here neat.
我倒不介意住在这里。真不错。

37
00:03:14,001 --> 00:03:19,440
Abandoned places are always fascinating especially when you're in saudi arabia and you don't expect to find one.
废弃地点总是很吸引人，特别是在沙特阿拉伯、你没想到会找到一处的时候。
